 are also weak, but F3 is the least valuable due to its lack of scoring relevance and poor integration into potential hands.\nReason: Discarding F3 minimizes loss of strategic potential since it cannot contribute to wind-based scoring patterns and is a dead tile in your hand. Keeping it risks blocking development of more promising combinations like chows in Bamboos or Characters. Among all valid discard options, F3 offers the lowest utility.\nAnswer: Play F3"}
